    "result": "## Summary\n\nI've successfully fixed the bug where `frai gate init --ci` was not creating the GitHub Actions workflow file.\n\n**The Problem:**\nThe `gate` command in the frai CLI (packages/frai-cli/src/index.ts) was only passing the variadic positional arguments to the frai-gate CLI, but not the flags like `--ci`. This caused frai-gate to receive only `init` without the `--ci` flag, so it skipped creating the workflow file.\n\n**The Fix:**\nI modified the action handler for the `gate` command to use `process.argv.indexOf('gate')` to find all arguments after the `gate` command and pass them directly to the spawned frai-gate CLI. This ensures both positional arguments and flags are properly forwarded.\n\n**Changes Made:**\n- Updated `/packages/frai-cli/src/index.ts` (lines 742-755) to:\n  1. Find the index of `gate` in `process.argv`\n  2. Extract all arguments after `gate` using `process.argv.slice(gateIndex + 1)`\n  3. Pass these complete arguments to the spawned frai-gate process\n\n**Verification:**\n\u2705 Running `node <repo>/packages/frai-cli/dist/index.js gate init --ci` now successfully creates both:\n- `FRAI-SPEC.md`\n- `.github/workflows/rai-gate.yml`\n\nThe workflow file contains the correct GitHub Actions configuration for running the Responsible AI Gate on every PR.",
